{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1503021-reading-for-scion-to-add-atmosphere","id":1503021,"title":"Reading for Scion to add atmosphere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-14T06:35:26-08:00","id":1503021,"title":"Reading for Scion to add atmosphere","content":"I've started my Scion campaign out in the Iron level, with leaning on the action movie trope as things advanced. I came across Harry Turtledoves Alpha and Omega recently, and tired using it as a baseline for peoples reactions as myth/religious ....effects start happening.<br /> <br /> I won't spoil, but the story takes people reacting to extraordinary events when an Relic in Scion's context is found, and then weirdness starts happening. Given the title, you can guess what form of artifact is found. Then consider what happens when the legends of the artifact start coming true.<br /> <br /> It's a pretty good book for the more mundane looking in, but it might also give ideas on how to handle the effects of items being found and possible effects on the over all gam","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13091-thewanderingjewels","name":"TheWanderingJewels","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13091_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T07:26:39-08:00","id":1503025,"title":"","content":"Sandman by Gaiman. It's built on the moods you want/need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T09:33:55-08:00","id":1503039,"title":"","content":"Frank Herbert's Dune series seems like it would be a good source of inspiration, since it involves humans--Paul and Leto II--developing god-like powers and coming to be revered as gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T17:21:30-08:00","id":1503086,"title":"","content":"Charles de Lint's books, set in present-day Canada, seem like a good fit. In <i>Greenmantle</i>, ordinary people encounter god-like magical beings (&quot;mysteries&quot;) as well as lesser spirits (&quot;secrets&quot;), while also dealing with the mafia. In the Tamson House series--<i>Moonheart</i> and <i>Spiritwalk</i>--Tamson House acts as a Gate between our world and what are essentially multiple Terrae Incognitae; ordinary people dwelling there encounter a range of spirits, minor and god-like, benevolent and malevolent. In <i>Someplace to be Flying</i>, god-like animal spirits are the main characters.<br /> <br /> The anime series <i>Kamichu!</i> is a slice-of-life story focusing on an unremarkable middle school girl who wakes up one morning to discover she has become a Kami. There's no real action (aside from a literal cat fight), though there is some adventure. But the story focuses on exploring her efforts to now living in both the human and spirit world and her friends' efforts to support her. One of those friends is the daughter of the local Shinto priest, who takes the main character under her wing and incorporates her into the rituals of the Shinto shrine, alongside the long-standing local god (who, at the start of the series, has run away).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T15:59:35-08:00","id":1503178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1503021-reading-for-scion-to-add-atmosphere?p=1503025#post1503025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sandman by Gaiman. It's built on the moods you want/need.</div> </div> </div> </div>His books Neverwhere and American Gods, also.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T12:32:49-08:00","id":1503338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1503021-reading-for-scion-to-add-atmosphere?p=1503178#post1503178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> His books Neverwhere and American Gods, also.</div> </div> </div> </div>Realistically, it is probably quicker to cite Gaiman's works that AREN'T useful then ones that are. <br /> <br /> That would be a bit silly though, so I'll add Good Omens and Norse Mythology (d'uh) to the list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T16:04:47-08:00","id":1503347,"title":"","content":"<b>Twilight of the Gods</b> a witty Victorian short story collection might be worth looking up. It's great at seeing the farcical aspects of the situation without denying the seriousness of the problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-14T13:16:21-07:00","id":1505367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1503021-reading-for-scion-to-add-atmosphere?p=1503338#post1503338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Realistically, it is probably quicker to cite Gaiman's works that AREN'T useful then ones that are.<br /> <br /> That would be a bit silly though, so I'll add Good Omens and Norse Mythology (d'uh) to the list.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few more:<br /> <br /> Anansi Boys<br /> The Ocean At The End Of The Lane<br /> The Graveyard Book<br /> His short story collections: Angels &amp; Visitations, Fragile Things, Trigger Warning","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T10:50:07-07:00","id":1505694,"title":"","content":"Sandman and American Gods by Neil Gaiman are a good choice for Scion style mood and you also could try some of Eric Brown Godpunk stories or even The Percy Jackson series if you don't mind that it's meant for a younger age group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}